# Pinned zenoh-c (Eclipse Zenoh's C binding of the Rust implementation), used
# by the asterism-zenoh gem (the CRuby Asterism::Zenoh).
# Same scheme as ZENOH_PICO_PIN of picoruby-asterism-zenoh:
# - At `gem install`, extconf.rb downloads the official prebuilt release for
#   the machine (asset.<platform> below) from <repo>/releases/download/<tag>/,
#   checks its sha256 and builds the extension against it
#   (ext/asterism_zenoh/zenoh_c.rb). `rake zenoh_c:fetch` does the same into
#   vendor/zenoh-c (gitignored) for working in the repository. Nothing is
#   built with Rust.
# - Upstream tag 1.10.1: the same number as zenoh-pico (the boards, pinned
#   in picoruby-asterism-zenoh) and the zenohd router used in the tests of
#   the Family mruby project. Zenoh keeps the wire compatible within 1.x;
#   keep them together anyway.
# - <platform> is <cpu>-<os> as ZenohCFetch.platform_key names this machine.
#   The sha256 values were computed from the downloaded archives and agree
#   with the digests GitHub lists for the release assets.
# - To update: bump the tag, the asset names and their sha256 here.
